WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:00.650
Hi, everyone.
大家好。

2
00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:08.050
It is Thanksgiving, and we are taking the week off, but we wanted to highlight an original Odyssey podcast, and we're going to feature it today.
正值感恩节，我们这周休息，但我们想重点推荐一档 Odyssey 原创播客，并将在今天播出。

3
00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:14.350
Yes, it is called Gone South, and it is an award-winning true crime documentary podcaSt.
没错，它叫《南方往事》（Gone South），是一档屡获殊荣的真实犯罪纪录片播客。

4
00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:22.650
Season four is out now, and it tells a different story about one of the South's most interesting crimes.
第四季现已上线，讲述了南方最引人入胜的犯罪故事之一。

5
00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:28.650
You can tune in every week as writer and host Jed Lipinski takes you through one of these crimes.
您可以每周收听，跟随编导兼主持人 Jed Lipinski 一起深入了解这些案件。

6
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:33.130
You will hear from the person who committed the crime, the person who solved it, or both.
您将听到犯罪者本人、案件侦破者，或者双方的讲述。

7
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:38.710
Gone South not only sheds fascinating insights into the criminal mind, but also into human nature.
《南方往事》不仅能带您深入洞察犯罪心理，还能让您对人性有更深的理解。

8
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:40.410
Enjoy this preview.
请欣赏这段预告。

9
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:50.850
If you ever have a chance to visit the Louisiana State Penitentiary, and I hope you don't, you'll notice something unusual on the way in.
如果你有机会去路易斯安那州立监狱参观——我希望你不会去——你会发现在入口处有些不同寻常的东西。

10
00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:56.030
Right outside the front entrance, there's a gift shop, a prison gift shop.
就在正门外，有一家礼品店，一家监狱礼品店。

11
00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:01.530
They sell various trinkets and posters, and you could even walk away with a t-shirt.
他们出售各种小饰品和海报，你甚至可以买件T恤带走。

12
00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:06.530
A t-shirt with a picture of the prison entrance, and a caption underneath that reads,
一件印有监狱入口照片的T恤，下面写着一行字：

13
00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.050
A Gated Community.
“封闭式社区”。

14
00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:16.550
Louisiana State Penitentiary sits on 18,000 acres, just south of the Mississippi border.
路易斯安那州立监狱占地 18,000 英亩，位于密西西比州边境以南。

15
00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:22.650
The prison is better known as Angola, because the land it occupies used to be a slave plantation,
这座监狱更广为人知的名字是“安哥拉”（Angola），因为这片土地曾经是一个奴隶种植园，

16
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:27.530
and a majority of the people enslaved there were taken from the West African country of Angola.
而那里的大多数奴隶都是从西非国家安哥拉被掳掠来的。

17
00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:34.330
The plantation became a prison in 1880, but an outside observer would have noticed almost no change.
该种植园在 1880 年变成了监狱，但外人几乎看不出有什么变化。

18
00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:36.930
Inmates lived in former slave quarters.
囚犯们住在以前的奴隶宿舍里。

19
00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.310
They worked the fields, just as slaves had.
他们像奴隶一样在田间劳作。

20
00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.390
They lived short and brutal lives.
他们的生命短暂而残酷。

21
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.550
Conditions hardly improved in the 20th century.
到了 20 世纪，条件几乎没有改善。

22
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:50.270
After a plague of murders, stabbings, and sexual assaults got the attention of the press in the 1960s,
在 20 世纪 60 年代，一系列谋杀、刺伤和性侵事件引起了媒体的关注，

23
00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:53.450
Angola was named the bloodiest prison in America.
安哥拉监狱被冠以“美国最血腥监狱”的称号。

24
00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:57.270
And it was almost impossible to escape.
而且，这里几乎不可能逃脱。

25
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.240
Angola is surrounded on three sides by the Mississippi River.
安哥拉监狱的三面被密西西比河环绕。

26
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.360
It's hemmed in on the other by dense, snake-infested swampland.
另一面则被茂密、毒蛇出没的沼泽地所阻隔。

27
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.260
Guards patrol the grounds on horseback, armed with 12-gauge shotguns.
狱警骑着马在场内巡逻，配备 12 号口径霰弹枪。

28
00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.860
Its layout is devilishly complex.
它的布局极其复杂。

29
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.780
Multiple outbuildings, barriers, and sniper towers are designed to prevent escapes.
众多的附属建筑、障碍物和狙击塔都是为了防止越狱而设计的。

30
00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.180
Even if an inmate did escape, they often drowned in the Mississippi's rushing currents,
即使囚犯真的逃了出去，他们也往往会淹死在密西西比河湍急的河流中，

31
00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.920
or succumbed to exposure, or got bitten by a rattlesnake.
或者死于恶劣天气，又或者被响尾蛇咬伤。

32
00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:33.200
And according to those who tried, a failed escape could be a fate worse than death.
据那些尝试过的人说，越狱失败的下场可能比死还惨。

33
00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.520
The punishment for escaping included months, if not years, in solitary,
越狱的惩罚包括数月甚至数年的单独监禁，

34
00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.720
or what inmates called the dungeon.
也就是囚犯们所说的“地牢”。

35
00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:44.580
Conditions one visitor in the 1970s described as medieval.
一位 20 世纪 70 年代的访客形容那里的条件简直是中世纪式的。

36
00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:52.060
And yet, in the 1980s, one inmate successfully escaped from Angola not once, but twice.
然而，在 20 世纪 80 年代，有一名囚犯成功地从安哥拉监狱越狱，而且不是一次，是两次。

37
00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.400
I don't know if you can even fathom it,
我不知道你能不能想象，

38
00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.380
but it's a big thrill when you successfully escape incarceration.
但当你成功越狱时，那种快感是巨大的。

39
00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.620
It's indescribable, man.
那感觉无法形容，伙计。

40
00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.660
Better feeling than any narcotic I ever had.
比我用过的任何毒品感觉都要好。

41
00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:07.240
I'm Jed Lipinski.
我是 Jed Lipinski。

42
00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.640
From Odyssey Podcasts, this is Gone South.
这里是 Odyssey 播客出品的《南方往事》。

43
00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.490
In this episode, I'm going to tell you the story of Jimmy Cox.
在这一集中，我将为你讲述 Jimmy Cox 的故事。

44
00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:20.690
You won't find any books, podcasts, or movies about Jimmy.
你找不到任何关于 Jimmy 的书籍、播客或电影。

45
00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.770
His story has never been told, at least not in that way.
他的故事从未被讲述过，至少不是以那种方式。

46
00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:28.270
I met Jimmy during the making of Gone South Season 2 about the Dixie Mafia,
我在制作《南方往事》第二季关于“迪克西黑手党”（Dixie Mafia）时遇到了 Jimmy，

47
00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:31.990
a loose-knit group of criminals who roamed the South in the 60s and 70s.
那是一个在 60 和 70 年代活跃于南方的松散犯罪组织。

48
00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:36.370
If you listened to that season, you probably remember a guy named Kirksey Nix Jr.
如果你听过那一季，你可能还记得一个叫 Kirksey Nix Jr. 的人。

49
00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.230
Unlike Jimmy, Kirksey is an infamous criminal.
和 Jimmy 不同，Kirksey 是个臭名昭著的罪犯。

50
00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.030
Some people believe he was the leader of the Dixie Mafia,
有些人认为他是迪克西黑手党的头目，

51
00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:43.770
though Kirksey disputes that.
尽管柯克西对此有异议。

52
00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.050
He's been locked up for over 50 years.
他已经被关了50多年了。

53
00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:50.170
When we were making that season, I had trouble getting in touch with Kirksey.
制作那一季节目时，我很难联系上柯克西。

54
00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.710
For months, my letters to him went unanswered.
几个月来，我写给他的信都石沉大海。

55
00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.650
Then I got an email from a guy named Jimmy Cox.
后来我收到了一封来自吉米·考克斯的邮件。

56
00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.870
Jimmy said he was a close friend of Kirksey's,
吉米说他是柯克西的挚友，

57
00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.010
dating back to the mid-70s when they'd served time at Angola together.
两人早在70年代中期就一起在安哥拉监狱服过刑。

58
00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:06.070
He told me Kirksey would be willing to speak with me if I spoke with Jimmy firSt.
他告诉我，如果我先跟他谈谈，柯克西就愿意接受我的采访。

59
00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:09.050
A week later, I was talking with Kirksey Nix.
一周后，我就和柯克西·尼克斯通上了话。

60
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.550
Jimmy made only a small appearance in Season 2 of our show,
吉米在我们的第二季节目中只露了一小脸，

61
00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:15.090
but I thought his personal story was worth telling.
但我认为他个人的故事值得一讲。

62
00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.470
I used to be a crime reporter for the Times-Picayune in New Orleans,
我曾经是新奥尔良《时代花絮报》的犯罪记者，

63
00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:19.830
and I'd been to Angola before.
我也去过安哥拉监狱。

64
00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:24.010
It was hard to imagine how someone could escape that place and live to tell the tale.
很难想象一个人怎么能从那种地方逃出来并活着讲述这段经历。

65
00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:25.790
We'll get there, don't worry.
我们会讲到那里的，别担心。

66
00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.790
But first, I want to tell you a little bit more about the escape artiSt.
但首先，我想多讲一点关于这位“逃脱大师”的事。

67
00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.500
Jimmy Cox grew up on the north side of Chicago in the 50s and 60s,
吉米·考克斯在50和60年代的芝加哥北部长大，

68
00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.340
the second youngest of 12 kids.
在12个孩子中排行倒数第二。

69
00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:43.060
His father had ties to the Chicago Mafia.
他的父亲与芝加哥黑手党有往来。

70
00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.620
So did some of his older brothers.
他的一些哥哥也是如此。

71
00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.220
He started hustling at a young age.
他很小的时候就开始干些偷鸡摸狗的勾当了。

72
00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:52.320
When we were little kids, I can remember we used to break into the freight trains,
我还记得我们小时候常去撬货运列车，

73
00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.660
and one time we broke in one that was full of beer.
有一次我们撬开了一节装满啤酒的车厢。

74
00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.200
We had beer stashed all over the neighborhood, different places.
我们在街区各处藏满了啤酒。

75
00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:05.080
And we didn't drink all of it, you know, but it was just fun to do it.
我们并没有把它们全喝掉，你知道的，但那样做很有趣。

76
00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.020
We stole a half a train car full of beer.
我们偷了半车厢的啤酒。

77
00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.420
And we're little kids.
那时候我们还是小孩子。

78
00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.780
I'm talking about 9, 10 years old, probably.
我是说大概才9、10岁吧。

79
00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.420
That was our mentality.
那就是我们的心态。

80
00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:19.540
And you've got to figure, I come from the area where you see gangsters walking around,
你要知道，我住的地方经常能看到黑帮分子走来走去，

81
00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:25.540
you know, nice clothes, diamond rings, driving nice cars, having nice women.
你知道的，穿着考究，戴着钻戒，开着豪车，身边美女如云。

82
00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:28.060
So that's what you aspire to.
所以那就是你向往的生活。

83
00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:34.250
When he wasn't robbing freight trains, young Jimmy shined shoes at a local social club where
不抢劫货运列车的时候，小吉米会在当地的一家社交俱乐部擦鞋，

84
00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.490
his father's friends hung out.
他父亲的朋友们常在那里消磨时间。

85
00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:40.750
A bunch of old Italian guys hung out in there and everything.
一群意大利老头子都在那儿聚会什么的。

86
00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:44.690
Well, I was allowed to go in and shine the shoes for them.
嗯，我被允许进去给他们擦鞋。

87
00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:45.990
That was my turf.
那是我的地盘。

88
00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:50.130
One of the gangsters who hung out at the club was a guy named Big Pauly.
在俱乐部混迹的黑帮分子中有一个叫“大保利”的家伙。

89
00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.610
Well, Big Pauly was the boss.
嗯，大保利是老大。

90
00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:56.750
And he'd sit in his barber's chair, and I'd shine his shoes.
他会坐在理发椅上，我就在那儿给他擦鞋。

91
00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:01.350
And when I'd get through, he'd reach in his pocket and pull out his big old roll of money.
等我擦完，他会伸手进兜，掏出一大叠钞票。

92
00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:05.090
And whatever bill was on the top, he would hold it over his shoe.
他会把最上面那张钞票举到鞋子上方。

93
00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:08.030
And if he could see his reflection, he'd give it to me.
如果他能从鞋面上看到自己的倒影，他就会把钱给我。

94
00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:10.310
So I was shining the shit out of those shoes.
所以我当时可是拼了命地把那些鞋擦得锃亮。

95
00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.990
One day I was down there shining them, and a dude reached over my shoulder.
有一天我正在那儿擦鞋，一个家伙从我肩膀上方伸过手来。

96
00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.890
I shot Pauly four or five times in the head.
我朝保利的脑袋开了四五枪。

97
00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:23.350
The old man hustled me out of there and told me, don't tell nobody nothing.
那个老头把我拽了出去，告诉我不准对任何人提起半个字。

98
00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:24.150
Just go home.
直接回家。

99
00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:31.150
I remember I used to keep my shoeshine box in the basement, and they had a big wash tub
我记得我以前把擦鞋箱放在地下室，那里有一个大洗衣盆，

100
00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:31.610
down there.
就在那儿。

101
00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.550
And I went down there, and I washed the blood out of my head.
我走过去，把头上的血洗干净了。

102
00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.950
I mean, there was stuff everywhere.
我是说，到处都是血。

103
00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:39.130
It traumatized me.
这给我留下了心理创伤。

104
00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.890
I ain't too proud to say that.
我不觉得承认这一点有什么丢人的。

105
00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:47.420
Jimmy says he never told anyone, including his dad, about what he'd seen.
吉米说他从未告诉过任何人，包括他父亲，他所看到的一切。

106
00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:51.440
He figured the guy who shot Pauly must have known him well enough to walk straight into
他认为那个枪杀保利的人一定和保利很熟，才能直接走进

107
00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:52.620
the shop unaccosted.
店里而没被阻拦。

108
00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:57.080
So therefore, I felt that I should never trust a soul.
所以，我觉得我不该信任任何人。

109
00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.240
And it was the catalyst to put me on.
这成了我人生转折的催化剂。

110
00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:05.600
If I felt that you were a threat, I was going to eliminate you first, because I wasn't going
如果我觉得你是威胁，我会先下手为强，因为我绝不会

111
00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:06.900
to let you eliminate me.
让你先干掉我。

112
00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.420
Jimmy dropped out of school in sixth grade.
吉米六年级就辍学了。

113
00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.980
He says he learned to drive by stealing cars.
他说他是通过偷车学会开车的。

114
00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:17.540
By his early teens, he developed a reputation as a solid getaway driver.
十几岁出头时，他已经成了小有名气的专业逃跑车手。

115
00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.460
These guys were going to do a bank job.
这些人打算去抢银行。

116
00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:25.020
They wanted three stolen cars, and they wanted me to place them in certain spots for them,
他们需要三辆偷来的车，还要我把车停在指定位置，

117
00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:25.200
right?
对吧？

118
00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:26.540
Switch cars, they call it.
他们管这叫换车。

119
00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.520
And I told them, I'll do the driving.
我告诉他们，我来开车。

120
00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:32.940
I was like 14 years old and made $17,500.
我当时大概14岁，赚了17500美元。

121
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.980
It was a lot of money back then.
在当时那可是一大笔钱。

122
00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.500
A whole lot of money.
非常大的一笔钱。

123
00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:47.300
In the late 60s, when Jimmy was in his early 20s, he moved to Hollywood, where his father
60年代末，吉米二十出头时，他搬到了好莱坞，他父亲在那里

124
00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.360
ran protection rackets for the local mob.
为当地黑帮经营保护费勒索生意。

125
00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.780
You know, Chicago people run L.A.
你知道的，芝加哥的人掌控着洛杉矶。

126
00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:55.120
Jimmy and his friends did errands and odd jobs for him and his associates.
吉米和他的朋友们经常帮他和他手下跑腿干杂活。

127
00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:02.080
One day, my dad told me, said, I want you to take your crew and go bust this Chinese restaurant
有一天，我爸跟我说，让我带上我的人去砸一家中餐馆，

128
00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.640
up right at lunchtime when it's most busy.
就在午餐时间，人最多的时候去。

129
00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:08.080
He said, just pull up front, go on with some baseball bats.
他说，直接把车停在门口，带上棒球棍进去。

130
00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.960
Don't hurt nobody if you don't have to.
如果没必要，别伤人。

131
00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:11.640
He said, but break shit up.
他说，但要把东西都砸了。

132
00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.520
Because the dude wasn't wanting to pay his street tax.
因为那家伙不想交保护费。

133
00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:20.480
So we jacked a limousine, pulled a limousine right up in front of it.
于是我们劫了一辆豪华轿车，直接开到了店门口。

134
00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:26.000
About four of us bailed out of it with baseball bats, went inside, started breaking up tables
我们四个人拿着棒球棍冲了进去，开始砸桌子，

135
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:30.240
and generally causing chaos and scaring the heck out of people.
制造混乱，把客人们吓得半死。

136
00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:34.120
And the guy got his mind right and started paying his taxes.
那家伙终于开窍了，开始乖乖交保护费。

137
00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:38.760
Before long, Jimmy was an established player in L.A.
没过多久，吉米就成了洛杉矶道上的一号人物。

138
00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:43.060
He bought a small nightclub near the corner of La Brea and Sunset and named it The We,
他在拉布雷亚大道和日落大道的交汇处买了一家小夜店，取名叫“The We”，

139
00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:46.920
spelled O-U-I, after the adult magazine of the same name.
拼写是O-U-I，取自同名的成人杂志。

140
00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:51.720
It was a place where hustlers could come in there at the end of the evening.
那是个骗子们在深夜可以去的地方。

141
00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:53.640
I had the cops paid off.
我当时已经买通了警察。

142
00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:59.120
You could buy cocaine right there at the table, a little glass vial for a hundred bucks,
你可以在桌边直接买到可卡因，一小瓶玻璃管装的只要一百块，

143
00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:02.180
and they'd bring it to you right with your drinks, you know?
他们会连同酒水一起给你送过来，懂吗？

144
00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:08.840
And it was a place for hustlers and thugs and gangsters to hang out and be comfortable.
那是骗子、暴徒和黑帮分子消遣和放松的地方。

145
00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:15.520
In L.A., Jimmy developed an addiction to heroin and PCP, and he had plenty of run-ins with the law.
在洛杉矶，吉米染上了海洛因和PCP的毒瘾，也多次与法律发生冲突。

146
00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:19.440
He was arrested for armed robbery, assault, and car theft, among other things.
他因武装抢劫、袭击和偷车等罪名被捕过。

147
00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:25.440
Yeah, it's hard to remember, but, you know, because I'd go to jail sometimes three times in one week.
是啊，很难记得清了，因为我有时候一周能进三次局子。

148
00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:33.880
But Jimmy always avoided significant jail time, until 1975, when he was sent to New Orleans to do a job.
但吉米一直没坐过太久的牢，直到1975年，他被派往新奥尔良去干一票。

149
00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:36.080
Jimmy told me what happened next.
吉米告诉了我接下来发生的事。

150
00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:39.940
It's a harrowing story, but he didn't want to go into it on the record.
那是个令人揪心的故事，但他不想在录音记录里谈论细节。

151
00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:43.480
Suffice it to say, the cops tracked him down in L.A.
简单来说，警察在洛杉矶找到了他，

152
00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:44.160
a year later
一年后，

153
00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:48.000
and charged him with robbery and two counts of first-degree murder.
并指控他犯有抢劫罪和两项一级谋杀罪。

154
00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:50.520
Jimmy's days as a flashy L.A.
吉米在洛杉矶当风光

155
00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:51.480
gangster were over.
黑帮的日子结束了。

156
00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:55.260
He was given two life sentences without the possibility of parole.
他被判处两次终身监禁，且不得假释。

157
00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:58.340
And since Jimmy's crimes were committed in New Orleans,
由于吉米的罪行是在新奥尔良犯下的，

158
00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:02.560
those life sentences would be served at the Louisiana State Penitentiary.
这些终身监禁将在路易斯安那州立监狱服刑。

159
00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:14.060
When Jimmy arrived in Angola in 1976,
1976年吉米抵达安哥拉监狱时，

160
00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:17.580
it had only recently been dubbed the bloodiest prison in America.
那里才刚刚被冠以“美国最血腥监狱”的称号。

161
00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.100
He remembers his first day inside.
他记得刚进去的第一天。

162
00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.460
When I got there and I'm walking to Chow,
我刚到那儿，正走去食堂，

163
00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:27.520
I noticed a kind of a little traffic jam down there,
发现前面有点交通堵塞，

164
00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.200
because it's a long, long walkway you have to walk.
因为那是一条很长很长的走廊，你必须走过去。

165
00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:34.060
You have to walk maybe almost a quarter of a mile to the Chow Hall.
你得走差不多四分之一英里才能到食堂。

166
00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:37.520
When I got up to where the traffic jam was happening,
当我走到堵塞的地方时，

167
00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:41.980
I noticed a dude was laying on the walk, all stabbed up,
我注意到一个人躺在过道上，浑身是伤，全是刀口，

168
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.000
and people were just stepping over him.
人们就直接从他身上跨过去。

169
00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.240
Wasn't paying him no mind, wasn't seeing if he needed, you know,
根本没人理会他，也没人看他需不需要，你知道的，

170
00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:49.240
to help if he was dead or what.
需不需要帮忙，或者看他是不是死了什么的。

171
00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:52.080
So that set the stage for me right there.
所以那一幕直接给我定了调子。

172
00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.580
And what did you think when you saw that?
那你看到那一幕时是怎么想的？

173
00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:55.860
What I thought?
我怎么想的？

174
00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:57.260
I'm in the jungle.
我进了丛林了。

175
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.280
Oddly enough, it was probably the safest time to be an Angola inmate
奇怪的是，那可能是安哥拉监狱100年历史上，

176
00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:03.880
in the prison's 100-year history.
囚犯最安全的一段时期。

177
00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:06.620
Between 1969 and 1974,
在1969年到1974年间，

178
00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:09.580
53 prisoners were murdered by other inmates.
有53名囚犯被其他囚犯谋杀。

179
00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:13.100
The federal government responded by instituting a series of reforMs.
联邦政府对此做出回应，实施了一系列改革。

180
00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.020
But Jimmy wasn't impressed.
但吉米并不以为然。

181
00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:18.500
And besides, he had only one goal in mind when he arrived.
再说，他刚到的时候只有一个目标。

182
00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:22.220
Your plan was always to escape, right?
你的计划一直都是越狱，对吧？

183
00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:23.340
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

184
00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:25.980
No human being is supposed to be confined.
任何人类都不应该被关起来。

185
00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.640
I don't even put my dogs in cages.
我连我的狗都不会关进笼子里。

186
00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:32.060
My main focus was on trying to get away,
我的主要目标就是想办法逃走，

187
00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.900
but we're sitting on an 18,000-acre farm
但我们身处一个18000英亩的农场，

188
00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:37.920
surrounded by the Mississippi on one side
一边被密西西比河环绕，

189
00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:41.020
and the Tunica Hills and panthers and bears
另一边则是图尼卡山，还有美洲豹、熊

190
00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:43.080
and rattlesnakes on the other side.
和响尾蛇。

191
00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:47.200
So I knew I had to do something with a little more finesse to it
所以我知道，我必须想出比单纯尝试

192
00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.040
than just trying to run through the bushes.
钻进灌木丛逃跑更巧妙的办法。

193
00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.060
Jimmy knew the stories of other men who tried to escape.
吉米知道其他尝试越狱的人的故事。

194
00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:56.420
In 1975, the year before Jimmy showed up,
1975年，也就是吉米到达的前一年，

195
00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:59.300
four men escaped after taking a prison guard hostage
四名男子劫持了一名狱警作为人质，

196
00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:02.300
and shooting another with a smuggled .22-caliber pistol.
并用一把走私进来的.22口径手枪射伤了另一名狱警后逃跑了。

197
00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.980
But bloodhounds for the prison's chase team quickly overtook them.
但监狱搜捕队的猎犬很快就追上了他们。

198
00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:09.220
Two of the men surrendered and were told to lay on the ground.
其中两人投降了，被命令趴在地上。

199
00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:11.200
According to one of the survivors,
据其中一名幸存者称，

200
00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:14.420
a guard executed them both with a submachine gun.
一名狱警用冲锋枪将他们两人处决了。

201
00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:16.800
The guard was never charged with a crime.
那名警卫从未被指控任何罪行。

202
00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:20.200
Jimmy spent his first four years at Angola
吉米在安哥拉监狱的前四年

203
00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:21.880
debating different escape strategies.
都在琢磨各种越狱策略。

204
00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.680
Then he found one he liked.
后来他找到了一个中意的。

205
00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:26.860
One day I was on the yard
有一天我在操场上

206
00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:29.720
and I walked up on these friends of mine talking
走近几个正在聊天的好友

207
00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.080
and they were talking about this guy
他们当时正谈论一个家伙

208
00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:35.440
that had just escaped from Charity Hospital in New Orleans.
刚从新奥尔良的慈善医院逃跑了。

209
00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:38.260
And I asked him, I said, well, how the hell he'd do that?
我问他们，我说，他到底是怎么做到的？

210
00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.680
And they said, well, they don't even hang.
他们说，他们甚至都不用吊着。

211
00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.320
They just shackle you to the bed and leave, Jimmy.
吉米，他们只是把你锁在床上就走了。

212
00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.280
I said, well, hell, I'm out of here.
我说，去他的，我这就走。

213
00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:46.560
How did he get there?
他是怎么去那里的？

214
00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:48.440
They said, well, he cut his eye.
他们说，他把自己的眼睛弄伤了。

215
00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:52.040
So I went and I tried to cut my eye.
于是我跑去尝试弄伤自己的眼睛。

216
00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:55.100
I even paid a guy to do it and it didn't work.
我甚至花钱雇人来做，但没成功。

217
00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.660
So I came back, did a little more research
所以我回来又做了一些研究

218
00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:00.160
and I got into the Grey's Anatomy
翻看了《格雷氏解剖学》

219
00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.540
to see where I could mess with it,
看看我能在哪里动手脚

220
00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:03.700
but I'm messing it up.
但我搞砸了。

221
00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:06.600
And I got these little medical drops
我弄到了一些医用滴眼液

222
00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:08.180
that numb your eye.
可以麻痹眼睛。

223
00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:10.160
I had a dude stick a needle in it.
我让一个家伙往我眼睛里扎了一针。

224
00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:13.340
The first part of Jimmy's plan worked.
吉米计划的第一部分成功了。

225
00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:16.160
He was sent to Charity Hospital in New Orleans for treatment.
他被送往新奥尔良的慈善医院接受治疗。

226
00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.180
He smuggled in a makeshift knife
他偷偷带进了一把自制小刀

227
00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:20.840
plus a key to open the handcuffs the guards on duty used.
还有一把能打开当值警卫所用手铐的钥匙。

228
00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:22.660
But when he tried to open the cuffs,
但当他试图打开手铐时

229
00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:23.640
the key didn't work.
钥匙没用。

230
00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:24.980
So Jimmy improvised.
于是吉米临场发挥。

231
00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:27.560
He asked the guard on duty to loosen the handcuffs,
他请求当值警卫松开手铐

232
00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:29.180
claiming they were cutting off his circulation.
声称手铐勒得他血液循环不畅。

233
00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.420
Then he slipped out of them when the guard left.
等警卫离开后，他便溜了出来。

234
00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:33.900
He took his neighbor's dirty clothes out of the hamper,
他从洗衣篮里拿出邻床的脏衣服

235
00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:34.980
put them on and waited.
穿上它们，然后等待时机。

236
00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:38.300
So after I got out of the handcuffs,
所以在我解开手铐后

237
00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:40.620
I got his clothes and put them on.
我拿了他的衣服穿上。

238
00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.380
I was laying underneath the covers,
我躺在被子下面

239
00:13:43.940 --> 00:13:46.340
fully dressed, a knife in my pocket,
穿戴整齐，口袋里揣着刀

240
00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:47.700
waiting to leave.
等待离开。

241
00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:49.360
But they had this older lady
但那里有一位老妇人

242
00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:51.240
that was always real nice to me.
一直对我非常好。

243
00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.000
And she came by and told me,
她走过来对我说

244
00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:55.620
says, Jimmy, I hate to see a nice young man
她说，吉米，我不忍心看到像你这样

245
00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:57.620
like you locked up like this.
好的年轻人被关在这里。

246
00:13:57.740 --> 00:13:59.060
And it's just not right.
这太不公平了。

247
00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:00.140
I said, well, you know, mom,
我说，好吧，你知道吗，大妈，

248
00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:02.000
I got the funniest feeling
我有一种很奇妙的感觉

249
00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.380
that I'm not going to be locked up all that longer.
觉得我不会再被关太久了。

250
00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:08.720
As soon as she left to go to the other ward,
她刚离开去另一个病房，

251
00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:09.820
I was gone.
我当时不在。

252
00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:14.230
Jimmy spent the next year and a half on the lamb.
吉米在接下来的的一年半里一直在逃亡。

253
00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:15.950
He moved from city to city,
他从一个城市搬到另一个城市，

254
00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:17.430
couch surfing, laying low.
借宿在朋友家，保持低调。

255
00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:19.310
When he got back to L.A.,
当他回到洛杉矶时，

256
00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.310
he moved in with a woman he dated years earlier.
他搬去和一位多年前约会过的女人同住。

257
00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:23.930
He didn't realize the feds had gotten to her firSt.
他没意识到联邦探员已经先找上她了。

258
00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:26.070
I went by her house
我去了她家，

259
00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:27.790
and they had feds in the house,
屋里有联邦探员，

260
00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:28.970
outside the house,
屋外也有，

261
00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:31.590
up in trees and everything else, I reckon.
树上到处都是，我想。

262
00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:33.190
Because they was everywhere.
因为他们无处不在。

263
00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:36.830
Jimmy returned to Angola in 1982.
吉米于1982年回到安哥拉监狱。

264
00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:38.370
His first day back,
他回来的第一天，

265
00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:39.430
he ran into the warden.
就撞见了典狱长。

266
00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:42.210
And he said, well, well, well,
他说，哎呀，哎呀，哎呀，

267
00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.150
we got Jimmy Cox back with us.
吉米·考克斯又回到我们这儿了。

268
00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:46.370
And I said, yeah, what happened, man?
我说，是啊，怎么回事，伙计？

269
00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.090
He said, what do you mean, what happened?
他说，你什么意思，怎么回事？

270
00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:50.530
I said, you guys are supposed to be protecting me
我说，你们不是应该保护我吗，

271
00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.450
and two people come in and kidnap me
结果有两个人进来，把我从那该死的医院里

272
00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.290
out that goddamn hospital, man.
绑架走了，伙计。

273
00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:57.370
And he started laughing, you know?
他开始笑，你知道吗？

274
00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:59.090
And he said, well, I'll tell you what,
他说，好吧，我告诉你，

275
00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:00.110
I'm going to send you someplace
我要把你送到一个地方，

276
00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:02.430
but you ain't got to worry about nobody kidnapping you.
保证没人能绑架你。

277
00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:04.450
And he sent me straight to Camp J.
然后他直接把我送到了J营区。

278
00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:10.020
Camp J was the prison's solitary wing,
J营区是监狱的禁闭区，

279
00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:11.920
Angola's equivalent of a supermax.
相当于安哥拉监狱的超高度设防区。

280
00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:14.320
It was two years before he was released
两年后他才被释放，

281
00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:16.100
back into the prison's general population.
回到监狱的普通监区。

282
00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.460
And yet, less than a month later,
然而，不到一个月后，

283
00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:21.100
Jimmy found himself back at Charity Hospital
吉米发现自己又回到了新奥尔良的慈善医院，

284
00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.680
in New Orleans with another eye injury.
眼睛又受了伤。

285
00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:26.580
As he told it, he'd poked himself in the eye
据他所说，是他在安哥拉监狱的医护人员换班时，

286
00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:28.940
when Angola's medical staff changed over.
自己戳伤了眼睛。

287
00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:31.480
They knew, but I mean,
他们知道，但我的意思是，

288
00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:33.500
they weren't in with the nuts and bolts
他们并不了解之前发生的事情的细节，

289
00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.400
of what had happened before, you know?
你知道吗？

290
00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.680
But this time, the staff at Charity were more vigilant.
但这一次，慈善医院的工作人员更加警惕了。

291
00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:42.980
Before, they had guards just come every two or three hours
以前，警卫每两三个小时才过来

292
00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:44.140
and check on you, right?
看你一次，对吧？

293
00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.460
But since my last escape,
但自从我上次越狱后，

294
00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.240
they started putting what they call a sit-down with you.
他们开始实行所谓的“贴身看守”。

295
00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:52.200
That means they have a guard sitting at the bed with you.
这意味着有一个警卫坐在你的床边看着你。

296
00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.900
Once again, Jimmy had smuggled a knife into the hospital.
吉米再次把一把刀偷运进了医院。

297
00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.640
At one point, he told the guard he needed a shower,
有一次，他告诉警卫他需要洗澡，

298
00:15:58.740 --> 00:15:59.780
and the guard obliged.
警卫照办了。

299
00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:04.740
And when he went down to take my shackles off my feet,
当他弯下腰去解开我脚上的镣铐时，

300
00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.080
and I put the knife to his throat and told him,
我把刀架在他的喉咙上，告诉他，

301
00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:08.780
I don't want to hurt you, I just want to go home.
我不想伤害你，我只想回家。

302
00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:11.880
I really didn't want to hurt the old man, you know?
我真的不想伤害那个老头，你知道吗？

303
00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.240
He tried to fight, so I wound up stabbing him
他试图反抗，所以我最后捅了他

304
00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:17.440
about 13 times, I think they said.
大概13刀吧，我想他们是这么说的。

305
00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:20.200
What saved me from killing him,
救了我一命，没让他死掉的是，

306
00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.360
I hit him one time in the chest,
我往他胸口捅了一刀，

307
00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:23.980
and I come in for the kill shot,
正准备补上致命一击时，

308
00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:26.940
but he had stuck both hands up over where I hit him at,
他把双手挡在了我捅的位置上，

309
00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.440
and the knife went through both hands,
刀穿透了他的双手，

310
00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:33.080
and it didn't have enough blade to penetrate any vital organ,
刀刃不够长，没能伤及任何重要器官，

311
00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.440
which was fortunate for me,
这对我来说很幸运，

312
00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:37.420
because I'd have been a dead cracker right now.
因为如果他死了，我现在就是个死白人了。

313
00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:38.720
They'd have executed me.
他们会处决我的。

314
00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:44.210
This time, Jimmy jumped out a window onto the fire escape,
这一次，吉米跳窗逃到了消防通道上，

315
00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:46.390
then exited the hospital through a side entrance.
然后从医院的侧门离开了。

316
00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:48.470
Less than a month later, he said,
不到一个月后，他说，

317
00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:50.610
he found temporary employment in New York.
他在纽约找了一份临时工作。

318
00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:55.850
In August of 84, I was sitting in the Bergen hunting fish club in Queens,
84年8月，我坐在皇后区的卑尔根钓鱼俱乐部里，

319
00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:59.370
enjoying a beer with a very infamous person.
和一个臭名昭著的人喝着啤酒。

320
00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:01.910
Can you say who that infamous person was?
你能说出那个臭名昭著的人是谁吗？

321
00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:03.090
Gotti.
戈蒂。

322
00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.410
That's Gotti, as in John Gotti,
就是戈蒂，约翰·戈蒂，

323
00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:09.330
head of New York's notorious Gambino crime family.
纽约臭名昭著的甘比诺犯罪家族的首领。

324
00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:12.470
Jimmy said he worked for John Gotti's crew for a few months
吉米说他在约翰·戈蒂的手下干了几个月，

325
00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:13.990
before relocating to Kentucky.
然后搬到了肯塔基州。

326
00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:16.150
After getting captured in L.A.,
在洛杉矶被抓后，

327
00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:18.350
he figured he'd try to hide out in a small town.
他想去个小镇躲起来。

328
00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:21.470
But Jimmy wasn't the type to stay cooped up in his house all day.
但吉米不是那种整天把自己关在屋里的人。

329
00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:28.190
Yeah, I'm driving a brand new El Dorado
没错，我开着一辆崭新的埃尔多拉多，

330
00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.730
with New Jersey license plates on it,
挂着新泽西的车牌，

331
00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:33.010
and then I had this little hot chick.
身边还带着个火辣的小妞。

332
00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:35.510
She's wearing fur coats and shit.
她穿着皮草大衣之类的东西。

333
00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:37.590
I was asking for it.
我这是自找的。

334
00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:39.370
According to Jimmy,
据吉米说，

335
00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:42.190
a nosy agent from the Kentucky Bureau of Investigation
肯塔基州调查局的一个爱管闲事的探员

336
00:17:42.190 --> 00:17:44.110
suspected him of robbing a local bank,
怀疑他抢劫了一家当地银行，

337
00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:45.490
which he claims he didn't do.
但他声称自己没做过。

338
00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:49.010
Either way, he came home one day to find himself surrounded again.
不管怎样，有一天他回到家，发现自己又被包围了。

339
00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:53.130
They had the state police, the FBI, and all them other idiots.
州警、联邦调查局，还有其他那些白痴全来了。

340
00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.530
When I seen him, I took off running.
我一看到他们，拔腿就跑。

341
00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:58.610
The dude jumped off a balcony and landed on my neck
那家伙从阳台上跳下来，压在我的脖子上，

342
00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:01.990
and stuck a little one of them little Mini-14s in my mouth.
把一把迷你-14步枪塞进了我的嘴里。

343
00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:03.630
Said, run now, run now.
他说，跑啊，现在跑啊。

344
00:18:03.710 --> 00:18:05.870
I said, well, get the gun out of my mouth, bitch, and I'll run.
我说，好吧，把枪从我嘴里拿开，婊子，我就跑。

345
00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:08.290
He didn't take it out of my mouth, though.
但他没把枪从我嘴里拿出来。

346
00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:12.960
At the time, Jimmy was carrying an ID that identified him
当时，吉米带着一张身份证，

347
00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:14.980
as James Aloysius Adams III.
上面写着詹姆斯·阿洛伊修斯·亚当斯三世。

348
00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:17.700
The cops assumed he was just a local gangster.
警察以为他只是个当地的混混。

349
00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.200
They didn't realize they had a two-time escapee
他们没意识到，他们抓到的是一个两次越狱、

350
00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.820
serving a life sentence at Angola.
在安哥拉监狱服无期徒刑的逃犯。

351
00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:23.720
After a preliminary hearing,
在初步听证会后，

352
00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:26.000
they made the mistake of taking Jimmy out of the courthouse
他们犯了个错，把吉米带出法院时

353
00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.580
without handcuffs or shackles.
既没戴手铐也没戴脚镣。

354
00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.100
He punched the jailer in the face and ran off.
他一拳打在狱警脸上，然后逃跑了。

355
00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:31.700
But in small-town Kentucky,
但在肯塔基州的小镇上，

356
00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:33.740
he was captured after just a few hours.
他没过几个小时就被抓住了。

357
00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:36.300
You know, them country towns, man,
你知道，那些乡下小镇，伙计，

358
00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.160
they was all on me like white on rice.
他们对我紧追不舍，就像苍蝇叮臭肉一样。

359
00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:41.920
Jimmy got seven years at the Kentucky State Penitentiary
吉米因这次越狱未遂

360
00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:42.840
for the escape attempt.
被判在肯塔基州立监狱服刑七年。

361
00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:45.180
Luckily, it was nothing like Angola.
幸运的是，那里和安哥拉监狱完全不同。

362
00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:49.040
When I went to Angola the first time,
我第一次去安哥拉监狱时，

363
00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:51.280
I was functionally illiterate.
基本上是个文盲。

364
00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:53.420
I could write you a note,
我能给你写张字条，

365
00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:55.420
put all the money in this bag,
把钱都装进这个袋子里，

366
00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:56.780
you know what I mean?
你懂我意思吧？

367
00:18:57.180 --> 00:19:00.520
But I couldn't write a formal letter.
但我写不出正式的信件。

368
00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:03.440
While I was in that prison in Kentucky,
在肯塔基州那所监狱服刑期间，

369
00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:05.960
they were real pro-education.
他们非常支持教育。

370
00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:08.520
I wound up getting a college degree,
我最终拿到了大学学位，

371
00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:10.300
a paralegal degree,
一个律师助理学位，

372
00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:14.600
and I was working on an addiction counseling degree.
当时还在攻读成瘾咨询学位。

373
00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:18.160
Jimmy met a prison psychologist
吉米遇到了一位监狱心理学家，

374
00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:19.620
who helped him process the trauma
她帮助他处理了

375
00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:20.900
he'd experienced as a kid,
他儿时经历的创伤，

376
00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:22.920
specifically Big Polly's murder.
特别是大波利的谋杀案。

377
00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:25.780
She was the very first person
她是我从11岁以来

378
00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:27.320
since I was 11 years old
第一个

379
00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:28.660
that I told that story to.
我向其讲述那个故事的人。

380
00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:30.900
She worked me through it.
她引导我走出了阴影。

381
00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:32.300
She told me, she says,
她告诉我，她说，

382
00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:33.920
you can't gauge your whole life
你不能仅凭一件事

383
00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:35.580
based on one incident.
就去衡量你的一生。

384
00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:38.420
We had a lot of conversations
我们进行了很多次谈话，

385
00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:39.440
and a lot of, you know,
还有很多，你知道的，

386
00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:41.440
it wasn't something that happened overnight,
这不是一夜之间就能解决的，

387
00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:44.760
but it was a major breakthrough for me.
但对我来说是一个重大的突破。

388
00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.980
It was like kind of shedding a whole lot of weight.
感觉就像卸下了沉重的包袱。

389
00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:51.760
A few years into his sentence,
服刑几年后，

390
00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.540
a close friend overdosed on heroin
他的一位挚友因海洛因过量死亡，

391
00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.000
that he and Jimmy were using together.
那是他和吉米一起吸食的毒品。

392
00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:57.280
Jimmy had been using heroin off and on
吉米说，他断断续续吸食海洛因

393
00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:58.760
for over 20 years, he says,
已经超过20年了，

394
00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.200
but he quit soon after.
但在那之后不久他就戒了。

395
00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:03.800
I just asked God a simple thing.
我只是向神祈求了一件简单的事。

396
00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:05.180
I said, God, I don't know how to pray,
我说，神啊，我不知道该怎么祈祷，

397
00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.500
but I'm just asking you
但我只是请求你

398
00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.800
to just relieve me of this addiction.
帮我摆脱这种毒瘾。

399
00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:12.200
And I started shooting heroin in 66, Jed.
我从66年开始注射海洛因，杰德。

400
00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:14.220
That was a long run, you know?
那真是一段漫长的岁月，你知道吗？

401
00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:17.120
I haven't touched narcotics.
我没有碰过毒品。

402
00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:20.000
I have a Louisiana medical marijuana card,
我有路易斯安那州的医用大麻卡，

403
00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:24.420
but I haven't touched any real narcotics since then.
但从那以后我就没碰过任何真正的毒品了。

404
00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:28.500
Jimmy changed while incarcerated in Kentucky.
吉米在肯塔基州服刑期间发生了改变。

405
00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:30.240
He got an education.
他接受了教育。

406
00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:31.480
He got clean.
他戒掉了毒瘾。

407
00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:34.000
He found a purpose in addiction counseling.
他在戒毒咨询中找到了人生的目标。

408
00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:35.940
But in 1993,
但在1993年，

409
00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:38.500
his sentence in Kentucky came to an end.
他在肯塔基州的刑期结束了。

410
00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:40.800
Jimmy was shipped back to Angola,
吉米被送回了安哥拉监狱，

411
00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:43.140
back to the bloodiest prison in America,
回到了美国最血腥的监狱，

412
00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:44.700
where he was due to spend
他本应在那里度过

413
00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:46.580
the remainder of his natural life.
余下的自然生命。

414
00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:55.060
When Jimmy returned to Angola in 1993,
当吉米在1993年回到安哥拉时，

415
00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:56.800
after 11 years away,
在离开11年后，

416
00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:58.720
he found it relatively unchanged.
他发现这里几乎没什么变化。

417
00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:00.420
He, on the other hand,
而他自己，

418
00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:01.720
felt like a different person.
却感觉像换了一个人。

419
00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:04.300
The change surprised many of his old pals.
这种改变让他的许多老朋友感到惊讶。

420
00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:06.640
I got back to Angola,
我回到安哥拉后，

421
00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:08.720
I kind of didn't get high anymore.
我基本上就不再吸毒了。

422
00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:12.300
A lot of guys were disappointed when I come back,
我回来时，很多人都很失望，

423
00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:13.660
because when they see me,
因为当他们看到我时，

424
00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:14.260
they said,
他们会说，

425
00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:15.020
oh man, good,
噢伙计，太好了，

426
00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.020
we have some good dope.
我们有好货。

427
00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:16.580
Now I said,
我说，

428
00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:16.840
nah,
不，

429
00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:18.360
I don't mess around no more, buddy.
我不玩那个了，哥们。

430
00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:20.480
And people couldn't believe it,
人们简直不敢相信，

431
00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:24.260
because my life had taken on a whole different lane,
因为我的人生已经走上了一条完全不同的道路，

432
00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:25.140
so to speak.
可以这么说。

433
00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:28.120
Not long after his return,
他回来后不久，

434
00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:31.000
director Steven Soderbergh shot a scene from his film
导演史蒂文·索德伯格在安哥拉监狱内

435
00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.820
Out of Sight Inside Angola.
拍摄了他的电影《战略高手》中的一个场景。

436
00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:36.000
The film follows the story of a charming bank robber,
这部电影讲述了一名迷人的银行劫匪的故事，

437
00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:37.100
played by George Clooney,
由乔治·克鲁尼饰演，

438
00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:38.560
who escapes from prison
他从监狱逃脱

439
00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:39.720
and kidnaps a U.S.
并绑架了一名美国

440
00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:40.200
marshal,
法警，

441
00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:41.660
played by Jennifer Lopez.
由詹妮弗·洛佩兹饰演。

442
00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:43.040
In the scene,
在那场戏里，

443
00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:44.780
George Clooney is planning his escape
乔治·克鲁尼正在食堂里

444
00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.440
with other inmates in the chow hall.
与其他囚犯策划他的越狱。

445
00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:47.620
According to Jimmy,
据吉米说，

446
00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:50.160
Soderbergh wanted real-life Angola inmates
